  "term": "operant learning",
  "definition": "In learning, operant learning refers to behavior changing as a function of its consequences, with behavior acquired and maintained under reinforcement contingencies. In the packet, it is described through operant conditioning principles such as continuous reinforcement, partial reinforcement, and extinction, where the schedule of reinforcement affects both acquisition and persistence of behavior.",
